# CODEOWNERS for godplans.
#
# This file routes pull-request review automatically. The current maintainer
# is @hannsxpeter; the default rule covers everything. The path rules below
# name the high-blast-radius surfaces, so a future co-maintainer can see at a
# glance which files reach users' machines and which gates guard the rest.
# When several rules match, the last one wins, so specific paths follow their
# directory.

# Default fallback: the maintainer reviews everything.
* @hannsxpeter

# The product: SKILL.md and the reference modules become standing instructions
# in every agent session that loads godplans, and steer every plan it writes.
/skills/godplans/ @hannsxpeter

# The Phase 1 usage-policy gate. Loosening it changes which projects godplans
# agrees to plan at all.
/skills/godplans/references/compliance.md @hannsxpeter

# The scripts that run inside users' projects. The validator is copied byte for
# byte into every plan as .godplans/validate-plan.sh and must run on stock
# macOS bash 3.2 and Linux; style-stats.py is copied the same way to
# .godplans/style-stats.py when a planned task runs it; the portable prompt
# saves plan-halflife.sh beside the validator. A regression here ships into
# plans that outlive the release.
/skills/godplans/scripts/ @hannsxpeter

# install.sh writes into users' home directories (~/.agents/skills,
# ~/.claude/skills, and equivalents) under POSIX sh.
/install.sh @hannsxpeter

# The meta-linter, the prompt builder, version sync, and the eval and release
# scripts. A lint check that stops failing silently removes a gate.
/scripts/ @hannsxpeter

# The gates' own configuration. package.json defines what npm run check and
# release:check run, and its description and keywords are the GitHub About
# text that release:check enforces. requirements/ pins the official skills-ref
# validator that CI installs and runs.
/package.json @hannsxpeter
/requirements/ @hannsxpeter

# Regression tests, including the lint self-test, and the behavioral eval
# cases and frozen evidence the README cites.
/tests/ @hannsxpeter
/evals/ @hannsxpeter

# CI workflows, Dependabot, and the issue and pull request templates.
/.github/ @hannsxpeter

# Plugin marketplace and plugin manifests. A manifest typo breaks
# /plugin install for every Claude Code user; lint checks their versions and
# plugin descriptions against SKILL.md and the marketplace tagline against
# package.json.
/.claude-plugin/ @hannsxpeter
/plugins/ @hannsxpeter
